PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round 0 view (A) reinforced by round 1: 5/7 colleagues select A on the basis that the LP fails both entity routes—own net assets unstated + all-owners test blocked by GP holding co (2538901 Ontario Inc.) whose shareholders are never shown to be AIs (mere gifting of $6 M does not establish ownership or qualification). B, C, D, E continue to clear at least one test each (spousal income >$300 k combined; exactly $5 M net assets satisfies “at least $5 M”; D $10 M and E $5.2 M entity-level net assets). 

Counter-arguments (cols 4,6,7) claim C fails because net assets land exactly on $5 M rather than above it; this is rejected—plain wording “at least $5 000 000” includes equality, and no guidance or valuation adjustment in the facts creates a shortfall. Col 4’s attempt to disqualify D/E on contribution vs. balance-sheet presentation is inconsistent with the stand-alone entity test language.

Key preserved evidence: NI 45-106 s. 1.1 (Jan 2021 Ontario) entity paragraph (q) requires every owner of an interest to be an AI; GP is a distinct interest-holder. Unresolved: precise regulatory interpretation of “at least” in net-asset test and whether any implied valuation haircut applies at exactly $5 M. Current view unchanged: A is the sole non-AI.}

